# Python-generated files
__pycache__/
*.py[oc]
build/
dist/
wheels/
*.egg-info

# Virtual environments
.venv

# Model checkpoints and evaluation splits live here. Neither is committed: the
# weights are ~2.2 GiB and the split is an upstream artifact. Both rules live at
# the repository root, and no file under either directory is ever tracked, so a
# checkout of an older revision cannot expose them to the snapshotter.
models/
data/

# No weight file and no checkpoint accessory may be committed, wherever it is
# dropped. The two directory rules above cover the documented locations; these
# format and filename rules are the safety net for a stray copy, which matters
# because the snapshotter only refuses files over 1 MiB -- a 313 KiB
# tokenizer.json would otherwise be committed silently. Deliberate, and nothing
# tracked today matches any of them: this repository holds no binary artifacts.
*.safetensors
*.gguf
*.ckpt
*.onnx
*.mlx
*.pt
*.pth
*.bin
*.msgpack
*.h5
tokenizer.json
tokenizer_config.json
chat_template.jinja
special_tokens_map.json
generation_config.json
vocab.json
merges.txt
